<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Italian War of Independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1848">1848</a>–<a href="/years/1849">1849</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Italian War of Independence was fought in 1848–1849 by the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> under Charles Albert, with volunteers from other Italian states, against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a>. Begun amid the revolutions of 1848, it ended in Sardinian defeats at Custoza (1848) and Novara (1849), after which Charles Albert abdicated in favour of his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-ii">Victor Emmanuel II</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-italian-war-of-independence.jpg" alt="First Italian War of Independence" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cesare Morbio (1812-1887) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Un_episodio_della_Battaglia_di_Novara.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section><h2 class="enc-section-title">Battles and settlements</h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-curtatone-and-montanara"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-curtatone-and-montanara.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Battle of Curtatone and Montanara</span><span class="tp">Battle · 1848</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-custoza-1848"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-custoza-1848.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Battle of Custoza (1848)</span><span class="tp">Battle · 1848</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
